      "label": 1,
      "status": "classified",
      "rationale": "`recv_object` deserializes bytes received from another process-group rank directly with `pickle.loads` (lines 510\u2013532), and this is used to reconstruct metadata received by `recv_tensor_dict` (lines 675\u2013679). Pickle can execute attacker-controlled reduction code, so a malicious or compromised peer in the group can trigger code execution; the sender helper's normal use of `pickle.dumps` does not make the receiver safe against forged peer messages.",
